{"type":"block","data":{"id":"achorestext1x10000000000000","parentId":"achorescard1000000000000000","rootId":"bchores00000000000000000000","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## How this works\n\n1. Connect an agent in Settings → AI: a program on this computer or a model on your API key. The folder it works in is chosen on the card, in its «Folder» field.\n2. Make a card and describe the task in it the way you would explain it to a person: what is needed, and how to tell it is done.\n3. Put an agent in the card’s «Who does it» field and drag the card into the «Agent prepares» column: the move is what starts the agent. If it has a question, the question appears on the card.\n4. When it finishes, the agent moves the card on itself, into the column whose name says what happened. What it made is in the folder.\n\nThis card can be deleted — it starts nothing.\n\nThe folder for this board is an ordinary folder on the computer: notes, lists, documents. The agent works in it and leaves what it did there too.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
